---
references:
  book:
    id: book
    type: book
    title: A Book
---

A field's value can be a **document** instead of text (§6.7). `;;…;;` is the
inline form: the payload is parsed and run through the page's own chain, and the
field carries the node list that run produced — the same fragment a
`{{{mdp[…] …}}}` binding writes, so no renderer had to learn a second shape.

A marker's extras head is a field position like any other, and the citation
inside it is the page's citation — one list, one numbering:

{{note}}@@noteAB{note: ;;lorem *ipsum*, a [[Wiki]] link and [^book];;}

An element's own positions take one too. `note` is preserved verbatim here, so
the value reaches the built-in `<a>` as a prop:

@[Card](/docs "Docs")@@anchorA{note: ;;Again [^book "p. 2"].;;}

The second citation of `book` keeps the number the first one was given, because
`citation_number` is an identity ordinal, not a counter of occurrences:

@[Slot](/docs)@@anchorA{body: ;;*value* in a spec position;;}
